>> title: Chocolate Pudding
>> category: Custards & Puddings
>> tags: chocolate, cocoa, pudding, stovetop, make-ahead
>> counters: Diner
>> servings: 6
>> time: 3 hr 30 min
>> slack: narrow — the starch needs a full two minutes at a real boil or it never sets, and it is whisked the whole time or the pan bottom catches

Whisk @granulated sugar{2/3%cup}(135 g), @cornstarch{3%Tbs}(24 g), @Dutch-process cocoa powder{1/4%cup}(21 g), @table salt{1/4%tsp} in a #saucepan{}.

>> step: whisk in the milk and yolks
Whisk @whole milk{2%cup}(480 mL), @heavy cream{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @egg yolks{3%large}(56 g) into @&(~1)dry mixture{} until smooth.

>> step: cook until it bubbles and thickens, 2 min
Cook @&(~1)mixture{} over medium, whisking, until it bubbles and thickens, about ~{2%min}.

>> step: stir in off the heat
Stir @bittersweet chocolate{4%oz}(115 g, chopped), @unsalted butter{2%Tbs}(28 g), @vanilla extract{1%tsp}(5 mL) into @&(~1)hot pudding{} off the heat.

>> step: strain, then chill 3 hr
Strain @&(~1)pudding{} into cups, press plastic wrap onto the surface, and chill for ~{3%hr}.
